
const descriptions = {
    fiveMinuteDungeon: "5-­Minute Dungeon is a chaotic, co-­operative, real-­time card game in which players have only five minutes to escape the randomized dungeon. Communication and teamwork are critical to survival because there's no time to form a carefully considered plan — and no predicting what dangers lie ahead.",
    sevenWonders: "You are the leader of one of the 7 great cities of the Ancient World. Gather resources, develop commercial routes, and affirm your military supremacy. Build your city and erect an architectural wonder which will transcend future times.",
    sevenWondersDuel: "In many ways 7 Wonders Duel resembles its parent game 7 Wonders. Over three ages, players acquire cards that provide resources or advance their military or scientific development in order to develop a civilization and complete wonders. What's different about 7 Wonders Duel is that, as the title suggests, the game is solely for two players.",
    sevenWondersDuelPantheon: "A pantheon from several civilizations — including Greek, Egyptian, and Middle-Eastern — gets added to 7 Wonders Duel in 7 Wonders Duel: Pantheon, with each god having its own power to help you or hinder your opponent.",
    aboveAndBelow: "Above and Below is a mashup of town-building and storytelling where you and up to three friends compete to build the best village above and below ground. In the game, you send your villagers to perform jobs like exploring the cave, harvesting resources, and constructing houses. Each villager has unique skills and abilities, and you must decide how to best use them.",
    agathaChristieDeathOnTheCards: "In Agatha Christie: Death on the Cards, which consists of a deck of eighty cards, players work co-operatively to solve a murder, using their detective skills to unmask the culprit and prevent their escape. The twist is that one of the players is the murderer and must work against the group to keep themselves hidden. Players also have dark secrets from their past they want to keep hidden from the other players. Who can you trust?",
    agricola: "In Agricola, you're a farmer in a wooden shack with your spouse and little else. At first, on a turn, your family gets to take only two actions, one for you and one for your spouse, as might be found among all the possibilities on a farm: plowing fields; collecting materials; building fences, and so on. There are numerous choices available, and while the game progresses you'll have more and more, as each round a new action card is flipped over, offering one more possible action. You might think about having kids in order to get more work accomplished but first you'll need to expand your house to make room - and what are you going to feed all the little rug rats?",
    airLandAndSea: "As Supreme Commander of your country's military forces in Air, Land, & Sea, you must carefully deploy your forces across three theaters of war: air, land, and sea. Air, Land, & Sea: Critters at War features the same gameplay as in Air, Land, & Sea, but with 100% critters and more vibrant colors.",
    alhambra: "Granada, 1278. At the foot of the Sierra Nevada mountains, one of the most exciting and interesting project of the Spanish Middle Ages begins: the construction of the ALHAMBRA. In Alhambra, players are acquiring buildings to be placed within their Alhambra complex.",
    alienFrontiers: "Do you have what it takes to be a deep space colonist? An alien frontier awaits the brave and daring! This new planet will be harsh, but if you have the skills to manage your resources, build a fleet, research alien life, and settle colonies, the world can be yours. Alien Frontiers is a game of resource management and planetary development for two to four players. During the game you will utilize orbital facilities and alien technology to build colony domes in strategic locations to control the newly discovered world.",
    amerigo: "In Amerigo, the players help Amerigo Vespucci on his journey to discover new land. The players explore the islands of South America, secure trading routes, and build settlements.",
    amongTheStars: "Among the Stars takes place in a war-ravaged galaxy where the warring alien races have declared peace in the wake of a threat with the potential to destroy them all. An Alliance is established to build space stations throughout the galaxy in order to promote trade among the races, strengthen diplomatic relations, and defend against this impending threat. Each player takes the role of one of those races trying to build the greatest space station. Through card drafting, the players select locations, and use these to build their station, scoring victory points based on the placement. The construction lasts four years, and the alien race with the most points at the end wins.",
    amunRe: "In Amun-Re, each pharaoh wants to build the most pyramids. To accomplish this, they must first acquire a province where they can trade and farm. With their profits, they can buy new provinces and building stones to erect pyramids. For all their actions, players must make clever use of their power cards and always offer appropriate sacrifices to Amun-Re.",
    anachrony: "It is the late 26th century. Earth is recovering from a catastrophic explosion that exterminated the majority of the population centuries ago and made most of the surface uninhabitable due to unearthly weather conditions. The surviving humans organized along four radically different ideologies, called Paths, to rebuild the world as they see fit: Harmony, Dominance, Progress, and Salvation. Followers of the four Paths live in a fragile peace, but in almost complete isolation next to each other. Their only meeting point is the last major city on Earth, now just known as the Capital.",
    applesToApples: "The party game Apples to Apples consists of two decks of cards: Things and Descriptions. Each round, the active player draws a Description card (which features an adjective like 'Hairy' or 'Shiny') from the deck, then the other players each secretly choose the Thing card in hand that best matches that description and plays it face-down on the table. The active player then reveals these cards and chooses the Thing card that, in his opinion, best matches the Description card, which he awards to whoever played that Thing card. This player becomes the new active player for the next round.",
    arboretum: "Arboretum is a strategy card game for 2-4 players, that combines set collection, tile-laying and hand management while playing in about 25 minutes. Players try to have the most points at the end of the game by creating beautiful garden paths for their visitors.",
    architectsOfTheWestKingdom: "Architects of the West Kingdom is set at the end of the Carolingian Empire, circa 850 AD. As royal architects, players compete to impress their King and maintain their noble status by constructing various landmarks throughout his newly appointed domain. Players need to collect raw materials, hire apprentices, and keep a watchful eye on their workforce. These are treacherous times, and rival architects will stop at nothing to slow your progress. Will you remain virtuous, or be found in the company of thieves and black marketeers?",
    arcs: "Arcs is a sharp, tactical space opera game set in a dark yet silly universe. Players represent officials from a distant, decaying and neglectful Empire who are now free to vie for dominance whether through battle, gathering scarce resources or diplomatic intrigue. Ready yourself for dramatic twists and turns as you launch into this galactic struggle.",
    arkhamHorror: "Arkham Horror is a cooperative adventure game themed around H.P Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos. Players choose from 16 Investigators and take to the streets of Arkham. Before the game, one of the eight Ancient Ones is chosen and it's up to the Investigators to prevent it from breaking into our world. During the course of the game, players will upgrade their characters by acquiring skills, allies, items, weapons, and spells. It's up to the players to clean out the streets of Arkham by fighting many different types of monsters, but their main goal is to close gates to other dimensions that are opening up around town. With too many gates open the Ancient One awakens and the players only have one last chance to save the world - defeat the Ancient One in combat!",
    arkhamHorrorDunwichLegacy: "Dunwich Horror is a large-box expansion for the Fantasy Flight Games edition of Arkham Horror, and is a part of the Arkham Horror Series.",
    arkNova: "In Ark Nova, you will plan and design a modern, scientifically managed zoo. With the ultimate goal of owning the most successful zoological establishment, you will build enclosures, accommodate animals, and support conservation projects all over the world. Specialists and unique buildings will help you in achieving this goal.",
    arkNovaMarineWorlds: "Ark Nova: Marine Worlds, an expansion for Ark Nova, introduces multiple new elements to the game, such as sea animals that each have to be played in new special enclosures that must be built adjacent to water.",
    automobiles: "Automobiles is a deck‑building game in which the fun is cubed — because instead of using cards to build a deck, you build with your collection of cubes. These cubes not only allow you to race your car around the track, but they also allow you to improve your handling, optimize your pit crew, and boost your speed, all of which are your keys to victory!",
    avalon: "Avalon is a card-based game where a line of 11 landscape cards form the board and the cards in your hand are made up of Knights and Enchantresses. There are 8 of each in each of five different colors, for a total of 80 cards, which both players share as a common draw deck.",
    azul: "In the game Azul, players take turns drafting colored tiles from suppliers to their player board. Later in the round, players score points based on how they've placed their tiles to decorate the palace. Extra points are scored for specific patterns and completing sets; wasted supplies harm the player's score. The player with the most points at the end of the game wins.",
    azulSummerPavillion: "In Azul: Summer Pavilion, players return to Portugal to accomplish the task that never began. As a master artisan, you must use the finest materials to create the summer pavilion while carefully avoiding wasting supplies. Only the best will rise to the challenge to honor the Portuguese royal family. Azul: Summer Pavilion lasts six rounds, and in each round players draft tiles, then place them on their individual player board to score points. Each of the six colors of tiles is wild during one of the rounds.",
    bananagrams: "Bananagrams is a fast and fun word game that requires no pencil, paper or board, and the tiles come in a fabric banana-shaped carrying pouch. One hand can be played in as little as five minutes. Much like Pick Two!, but without the letter values. Using a selection of 144 plastic letter tiles in the English edition, each player works independently to create their own 'crossword' faster than one's opponents. When a player uses up all their letters, all players take a new tile from the pool. The object of the game is to be the first to complete a word grid after the 'bunch' of tiles has been depleted.",
    baseballHighlights2045: "In this quick and interactive game, two players build their teams as they play, combining both strategy (building your team) and tactics (playing the game) without any of the downtime. During each 'mini-game', each player alternates playing six cards to simulate a full game's highlights. The mini-game includes defensive and offensive actions, and your single card play may include elements of defensive and/or offensive plays. Do you try to thwart your opponent's pending hits, put up strong offensive action of your own, or use your better players to do both? Players buy new free agents after each mini-game to improve their roster, and the team who wins the most mini-games in the series is the champ!",
    battleStarGalactica: "Battlestar Galactica: The Board Game is a game of mistrust, intrigue, and the struggle for survival. Based on the Sci Fi Channel series, Battlestar Galactica: The Board Game puts players in the role of one of ten of their favorite characters from the show. Each playable character has their own abilities and weaknesses, and must all work together in order for humanity to have any hope of survival. However, one or more players in every game secretly side with the Cylons. Players must attempt to expose the traitor while fuel shortages, food contaminations, and political unrest threatens to tear the fleet apart.",
    betrayalAtHouseOnTheHill: "Betrayal at House on the Hill is a tile game that allows players to lay out the haunted house room by room, tile by tile, creating a new thrilling game board every time. The game is designed for three to six people, each of whom plays one of six possible characters. Secretly, one of the characters betrays the rest of the party, and the innocent members of the party must defeat the traitor in their midst before it’s too late! Betrayal at House on the Hill will appeal to any game player who enjoys a fun, suspenseful, and strategic game.",
    betweenTwoCastlesOfMadKingLudwig: "Between Two Castles of Mad King Ludwig is a competitive tile-drafting game in which each tile is a room in a castle. You work together with the player on your left to design one castle, and with the player on your right on another castle. On each turn you select two tiles from your hand, reveal them, then work with your partners to place them. To win, you have to share your attention and your devotion between two castles.",
    betweenTwoCities: "Between Two Cities is a 30-minute tile-drafting game for 1-7 players in which each tile is part of a city. You work with the player on your left to build one city center while simultaneously working with the player on your right to build a second city center. On each turn you select two tiles from your hand, reveal them, then work with your partners to place one of your selected tiles into each of your two cities.",
    bloodborneTheCardGame: "Bloodborne: The Card Game is based on the Chalice Dungeons in the video game Bloodborne — the ever-changing labyrinths and tombs carved out by the Great Ones beneath the fallen city of Yharnam, where horrifying creatures reside. Players compete to kill monsters and take their blood.",
    bloodOnTheClocktower: "Blood on the Clocktower is a bluffing game with players on opposing teams of Good and Evil, overseen by a Storyteller player who conducts the action and makes crucial decisions. The goal of the game is to successfully deduce and execute the demon and their minions before they outnumber the townsfolk.",
    bloodRage: "In Blood Rage, players control the warriors, leader, and ship of their own Viking clan. Ragnarök has come and it’s the end of the world! It’s the Vikings’ last chance to go down in a blaze of glory and secure their places in Valhalla at Odin’s side! As a Viking you can pursue one of many pathways to glory. You can: invade and pillage the land for its rewards; crush your opponents in battle: fulfill quests: increase your clan's stats: or even die gloriously in battle or from Ragnarök, the ultimate inescapable doom.",
    bobRossArtOfChillGame: "If you want to paint with Bob Ross, you need to be chill, so whoever reaches maximum chill first in Bob Ross: Art of Chill Game wins.",
    bohnanza: "In this game, you plant, then harvest bean cards in order to earn coins. Each player starts with a hand of random bean cards, and each card has a number on it corresponding to the number of that type of beans in the deck. Unlike in most other card games, you can't rearrange the order of cards in hand, so you must use them in the order that you've picked them up from the deck — unless you can trade them to other players, which is the heart of the game.",
    brassBirmingham: "Brass: Birmingham is an economic strategy game sequel to Martin Wallace's 2007 masterpiece, Brass. This game tells the story of competing entrepreneurs in Birmingham during the industrial revolution between the years of 1770 and 1870.",
    brassLancashire: "Brass: Lancashire — first published as Brass — is an economic strategy game that tells the story of competing cotton entrepreneurs in Lancashire during the industrial revolution. You must develop, build and establish your industries and network so that you can capitalize on demand for iron, coal and cotton. The game is played over two halves: the canal phase and the rail phase. To win the game, score the most victory points (VPs), which are counted at the end of each phase.",
    bulletStar: "Assume the role of the universes' most powerful heroines as you settle their disputes with excessive firepower! Use actions to form patterns, clear bullets from your sight, and bombard the opponent! Deal with the curtain of bullets coming at you each round and be the last heroine standing to win!",
    bunnyKingdom: "Peace has come at last to the great Bunny Kingdom! Lead your clan of rabbits to glory by gathering resources and building new cities across the land!",
    bunnyKingdomInTheSky: "Rabbit settlers fanning out across the New World are organizing into Districts, and trade has begun to flourish. Play your cards right and profit from the situation! This expansion adds a second board, a full set of pink rabbits to play with a 5th fellow bunny-lover, new cards and a new building : the Carrotadel!",
    burgleBros: "Burgle Bros. is a cooperative game. Players are unique members of a crew trying to pull off a robbery of a highly secure building — without getting caught.",
    calico: "In Calico, players compete to sew the coziest quilt as they collect and place patches of different colors and patterns. Each quilt has a particular pattern that must be followed, and players are also trying to create color and pattern combinations that are not only aesthetically pleasing, but also able to attract the cuddliest cats!",
    canvas: "In Canvas, you play as a painter competing in an art competition. Players will collect art cards, layering 3 of them together to create their own unique Painting. Each card contains a piece of artwork as well as a set of icons used during scoring. Icons will be revealed or hidden based on the way players choose to layer the cards making for an exciting puzzle. Paintings are scored based on a set of Scoring cards which will change each game. Once players have created and scored 3 paintings the game ends.",
    captainSonar: "In Captain Sonar, you and your teammates control a state-of-the-art submarine and are trying to locate an enemy submarine in order to blow it out of the water before they can do the same to you. Every role is important, and the confrontation is merciless. Be organized and communicate, because a captain is nothing without his crew: the Chief Mate, the Radio Operator, and the Engineer",
    carcassonne: "Carcassonne is a tile placement game in which the players draw and place a tile with a piece of southern French landscape represented on it. The tile might feature a city, a road, a cloister, grassland or some combination thereof, and it must be placed adjacent to tiles that have already been played, in such a way that cities are connected to cities, roads to roads, et cetera.",
    cascadia: "In Cascadia, you take turns building out your own terrain area and populating it with wildlife. You start with three hexagonal habitat tiles (with the five types of habitat in the game), and on a turn you choose a new habitat tile that's paired with a wildlife token, then place that tile next to your other ones and place the wildlife token on an appropriate habitat.",
    castlesOfMadKingLudwig: "In the tile-laying game Castles of Mad King Ludwig, players are tasked with building an amazing, extravagant castle for King Ludwig II of Bavaria...one room at a time. You see, the King loves castles, having built Neuschwanstein (the castle that inspired the Disney theme park castles) and others, but now he's commissioned you to build the biggest, best castle ever — subject, of course, to his ever-changing whims.",
    catan: "In Catan (formerly The Settlers of Catan), players try to be the dominant force on the island of Catan by building settlements, cities and roads. On each turn dice are rolled to determine which resources the island produces. Players build structures by 'spending' resources (sheep, wheat, wood, brick and ore) which are represented by the relevant resource cards; each land type, with the exception of the unproductive desert, produces a specific resource: hills produce brick, forests produce wood, mountains produce ore, fields produce wheat, and pastures produce sheep.",
    catanStarfarers: "Twenty years ago, the settlers started into the depths of the galaxy to discover unknown planets, the undiscovered universe lying before them. Maybe they'll find planets with good ore or carbon deposits — or perhaps only barren ice planets. They might encounter alien folks and start lucrative trading, with pirates and wormholes being a constant challenge for them.",
    catInTheBox: "Cat in the Box is the quintessential quantum trick-taking card game for 2 - 5 cool cats, where your card’s color isn’t defined until you play it! Hypothesize how many tricks you will win, and record your bid. Place tokens on the community research board as you play your hand, and connect large groups of tokens to score even more points. Plan your tricks carefully as you cannot claim the color of a card with the same number that has already been declared. Doing so would be pawsitively catastrophic as you have just created a paradox!",
    championsOfMidgard: "Champions of Midgard is a middleweight, Viking-themed, worker placement game with dice rolling in which players are leaders of Viking clans who have traveled to an embattled Viking harbor town to help defend it against the threat of trolls, draugr, and other mythological Norse beasts. By defeating these epic creatures, players gain glory and the favor of the gods. When the game ends, the player who has earned the most glory earns the title of Jarl and is recognized as a champion of Midgard!",
    chess: "Chess is game that needs no introduction, but we'll give it one anyway! Chess is a two-player, abstract strategy board game that represents medieval warfare on an 8x8 board with alternating light and dark squares. Opposing pieces, traditionally designated White and Black, are initially lined up on either side of the board. Each type of piece has a unique form of movement and capturing occurs when a piece, via its movement, occupies the square of an opposing piece. Players take turns moving one of their pieces in an attempt to capture, attack, defend, or develop their positions. Chess games can end in checkmate (when the king cannot escape from the opponent's pieces), resignation (when one player recognizes that defeat is inevitable and ends the game), or one of several types of draws.",
    citiesOfSplendor: "Cities of Splendor is a quartet of expansions for use with the Splendor base game. Each expansion is added to the basic game and they should be played separately.",
    cityOfGears: "City of Gears is a unique steampunk game of exploration, area control, worker placement, and engine building. From your incredible Factory, you must race to claim ownership over the magnificent ruins of an abandoned clockwork metropolis. Each game plays in under an hour, and because only nine of the city tiles (from dozens available) are randomly chosen and placed each game, no two games ever play the same.",
    cityOfIron: "In City of Iron, 2-4 players compete to build up a small nation in a world of machines, magic, and money. Become the leader of one of four rival nations: the industrious humans, the toad engineers, the scholarly Cresarians, or the clever hogmen. Produce goods like machine parts and bottled demons to gain wealth, or research steam-age technology and recruit mercenaries to control the continent.",
    clank: "Burgle your way to adventure in the deck-building board game Clank! Sneak into an angry dragon's mountain lair to steal precious artifacts. Delve deeper to find more valuable loot. Acquire cards for your deck and watch your thievish abilities grow. Be quick and be quiet. One false step and CLANK! Each careless sound draws the attention of the dragon, and each artifact stolen increases its rage. You can enjoy your plunder only if you make it out of the depths alive!",
    clue: "Clue is a murder mystery game. The aim is to find out who committed the murder, which weapon they used, and where in the mansion they did it. How do you solve the case? By careful questioning of your fellow players you can deduce which information is concealed in the crime envelope. The trick is to be clever with your questioning. Everyone develops their own system!",
    cockroachPoker: "Cockroach Poker is a reverse set collection game that has nothing to do with poker – except that the game is all about bluffing, with cards that show cockroaches, rats and stink bugs. The goal is to force another player to collect 4 of any one type of critter.",
    codenames: "Two rival spymasters know the secret identities of 25 agents. Their teammates know the agents only by their codenames — single-word labels like \"disease\", \"Germany\", and \"carrot\". Yes, carrot. It's a legitimate codename. Each spymaster wants their team to identify their agents first...without uncovering the assassin by mistake.",
    concept: "In Concept, your goal is to guess words through the association of icons. A team of two players – neighbors at the table – choose a word or phrase that the other players need to guess. Acting together, this team places pieces judiciously on the available icons on the game board.",
    concordia: "Concordia is a peaceful, strategy game of economic development in Roman times for 2-5 players aged 13 and up. Instead of looking to the luck of dice or cards, players must rely on their strategic abilities. Be sure to watch your rivals to determine which goals they are pursuing and where you can outpace them! In the game, colonists are sent out from Rome to settle down in cities that produce bricks, food, tools, wine, and cloth. Each player starts with an identical set of playing cards and acquires more cards during the game.",
    cosmicEncounter: "In Cosmic Encounter, each player becomes the leader of one of dozens of alien races, each with its own unique power. On a player's turn, he or she becomes the offense. The offense encounters another player on a planet by moving a group of his or her ships through the hyperspace gate to that planet. Both sides can invite allies and play cards to try and tip the encounter in their favor.",
    coup: "In Coup, you want to be the last player with influence in the game, with influence being represented by face-down character cards in your playing area.",
    cryptid: "Cryptid is a unique deduction game of honest misdirection in which players must try to uncover information about their opponents' clues while throwing them off the scent of their own. Each player holds one piece of evidence to help them find the creature, and on their turn they can try to gain more information from their opponents. Be warned; give too much away and your opponents might beat you to the mysterious animal and claim the glory for themselves!",
    cthulhuWars: "Cthulhu Wars is a strategy boardgame in which the players take the part of alien races and gods taken from the Cthulhu mythos created by H. P. Lovecraft. The game is physically large, and includes sixty-four figurines of the cultists, monsters, aliens, and Great Old Ones that range in height from approximately 20 mm to nearly 180 mm.",
    cthulhuWarsTchoTcho: "The Tcho-Tcho Expansion adds a new faction to Cthulhu Wars. The Tcho-Tchos are a human-based faction representing the physically advanced, but ethically repulsive. The Tcho-Tcho tribe has the ability to interfere with other players by worshipping their Great Old Ones!",
    cyclades: "In this latest collaboration between Bruno Cathala and Ludovic Maublanc, players must buy the favor of the gods in their race to be the first player to build two cities in the Ancient Greek island group known as the Cyclades.",
    darkestNight: "Darkest Night, by designer Jeremy Lennert, is a fully-cooperative board game for one to four players (up to six with variants), set in a kingdom broken under a necromancer’s shadow. Each player takes on the role of one of the kingdom’s last heroes (nine playable characters), each with a unique set of special abilities, just as they hatch a plan to save the realm.",
    daybreak: "Daybreak is a co-operative game about climate action. Each player controls a world power, deploying policies and technologies to both dismantle the engine of global heating and to build resilient societies that protect people from life-threatening crises.",
    deadOfWinter: "\"Crossroads\" is a game series from Plaid Hat Games that tests a group of survivors' ability to work together and stay alive while facing crises and challenges from both outside and inside. Dead of Winter: A Crossroads Game, the first title in this series, puts 2-5 players in a small, weakened colony of survivors in a world in which most of humanity is either dead or diseased, flesh-craving monsters. Each player leads a faction of survivors, with dozens of different characters in the game.",
    decksOfCards: "Simple, classic, and no explanation needed. With one or more decks of cards, the possibilities are endless.",
    decorum: "Décorum is a cooperative, hidden information game where you and your partner share the same objective: decorate your home in a way that makes you both happy. The problem is, different things make each of you happy and nobody says exactly what they need. Can you find a happy compromise, or is it time to move out?!",
    diceCity: "Dice City is a \"dice-crafting\" game in which the locations in your city act as the changing faces of your dice each turn. Use tactics and strategy to press your claim!",
    diceForge: "Dice Forge is a development game featuring innovative mechanics based on dice with removable faces. In this dice crafting game, players build their own dice. Roll your dice, manage your resources, complete ordeals before your opponents and explore multiple winning strategies.",
    dinosaurIsland: "In Dinosaur Island, players will have to collect DNA, research the DNA sequences of extinct dinosaur species, and then combine the ancient DNA in the correct sequence to bring these prehistoric creatures back to life. Dino cooking! All players will compete to build the most thrilling park each season, and then work to attract (and keep alive!) the most visitors each season that the park opens.",
    dixitOdyssey: "Game play in Dixit Odyssey matches that of Dixit: Each turn one player is the storyteller. This player secretly chooses one card in his hand, then gives a word or sentence to describe this card—but not too obviously. Each other player chooses a card in hand that matches this word/sentence and gives it to the storyteller. The storyteller then lays out the cards, and all other players vote on which card belongs to the storyteller. If no one or everyone guesses the storyteller's card, the storyteller receives no points and all players receive two; otherwise the storyteller and the correct guesser(s) each receive three points. Players score one point for each vote their image receives. Players refill their hands, and the next player becomes the storyteller. When the deck runs out, the player with the most points wins.",
    dominion: "In Dominion, each player starts with an identical, very small deck of cards. In the center of the table is a selection of other cards the players can \"buy\" as they can afford them. Through their selection of cards to buy, and how they play their hands as they draw them, the players construct their deck on the fly, striving for the most efficient path to the precious victory points by game end.",
    dominionAllies: "Dominion: Allies, the 14th expansion in the Dominion series, contains 400 cards, with 31 new Kingdom card piles that contain allies who will do favors for you and split piles that you can rotate",
    dominionDarkAges: "Dominion: Dark Ages is the seventh addition to the game of Dominion. It contains 500 cards but is not a standalone game. It adds 35 new Kingdom cards to Dominion, plus new bad cards you give to other players (Ruins), new cards to replace starting Estates (Shelters), and cards you can get only via specific other cards. The central themes are the trash and upgrading. There are cards that do something when trashed, cards that care about the trash, cards that upgrade themselves, and ways to upgrade other cards.",
    dominionSeaside: "Dominion: Seaside is an expansion to both Dominion and Dominion: Intrigue. As such, it does not contain material for a complete game.",
    dontBreakTheIce: "Tap out ice blocks one by one. They won't melt when you are done! Take your time and do some thinking to keep the polar bear from sinking. To win, the bear must stay on top. One wrong block-he'll go ker-plop!",
    dune: "In Dune you will become the leader of one of six great factions. Each wishes to control the most valuable resource in the universe - melange, the mysterious spice only found at great cost on the planet DUNE. As Duke Leto Atreides says “All fades before melange. A handful of spice will buy a home on Tupile. It cannot be manufactured, it must be mined on Arrakis. It is unique and it has true geriatric properties.” And without melange space travel would be impossible. Only by ingesting the addictive drug can the Guild Steersman continue to experience visions of the future, enabling them to plot a safe path through hyperspace.",
    duneImperium: "Dune: Imperium is a game that uses deck building to add a hidden information angle to traditional worker placement. It finds inspiration in elements and characters from the Dune legacy, both the new film from Legendary Pictures and the seminal literary series from Frank Herbert, Brian Herbert, and Kevin J. Anderson.",
    eclipse: "A game of Eclipse places you in control of a vast interstellar civilization, competing for success with its rivals. You explore new star systems, research technologies, and build spaceships with which to wage war. There are many potential paths to victory, so you need to plan your strategy according to the strengths and weaknesses of your species, while paying attention to the other civilizations' endeavors.",
    eldritchHorror: "Eldritch Horror is a co-operative game of terror and adventure in which one to eight players take the roles of globetrotting investigators working to solve mysteries, gather clues, and protect the world from an Ancient One - that is, an elder being intent on destroying our world. Each Ancient One comes with its own unique decks of Mystery and Research cards, which draw you deeper into the lore surrounding each loathsome creature. Discover the true name of Azathoth or battle Cthulhu on the high seas.",
    eldritchHorrorMountainsOfMadness: "Explore the farthest reaches of Antarctica in Mountains of Madness, the second expansion for Eldritch Horror. Inspired by H.P. Lovecraft's novella, this expansion allows you to trace the path of a doomed expedition and enter the immense City of the Elder Things. What happens in Antarctica has worldwide repercussions as freshly-awakened horrors spread across the globe.",
    everdell: "Within the charming valley of Everdell, beneath the boughs of towering trees, among meandering streams and mossy hollows, a civilization of forest critters is thriving and expanding. From Everfrost to Bellsong, many a year have come and gone, but the time has come for new territories to be settled and new cities established. You will be the leader of a group of critters intent on just such a task. There are buildings to construct, lively characters to meet, events to host—you have a busy year ahead of yourself. Will the sun shine brightest on your city before the winter moon rises?",
    everdellBellfaire: "The king is throwing an unprecedented year-long event to commemorate the 100th year since Everdell's founding. Come one, come all, to the Bellfaire! Bellfaire is a new expansion for Everdell that offers several different gameplay modules, including: components and rules for 5-6 players, player powers and resource boards, a Bellfaire board with a new Market location, Garland Awards, which are shared endgame goals, and new Special Event cards.",
    everdellNewLeaf: "Everdell's bustling city Newleaf has just opened its first train station, and many new critters and big ideas are rolling in. Newleaf introduces brand new critters, constructions, and exciting events to draw Visitor cards to your blossoming city! It also features the Train Station Board, resource-delivering Train Cars, travel-worthy Tickets, and Reservation Tokens!",
    evolution: "In Evolution, players adapt their species in a dynamic ecosystem where food is scarce and predators lurk. Traits like Hard Shell and Horns will protect your species from Carnivores, while a Long Neck will help them get food that others cannot reach. With over 4,000 ways to evolve your species, every game becomes a different adventure.",
    explodingKittens: "Exploding Kittens is a kitty-powered version of Russian Roulette. Players take turns drawing cards until someone draws an exploding kitten and loses the game. The deck is made up of cards that let you avoid exploding by peeking at cards before you draw, forcing your opponent to draw multiple cards, or shuffling the deck.",
    fitToPrint: "Fit to Print is a tile-laying game for the whole family. Players simultaneously collect newspaper tiles, stacking them on their desks until they think they have what they need to make the perfect front page. Then, they will yell “Layout!” and begin to lay out the page by carefully considering the placement of centerpieces, articles, photographs, and advertisements. When everything is just right, they yell “Print” to be the first off the press and gain their choice of centerpiece for the next round! This hectic spatial puzzle features over 100 unique newspaper tiles, six characters with their own special abilities, as well as three decks of Breaking News cards — so that each and every time you play you will be solving a new puzzle!",
    fiveTribes: "Designed by Bruno Cathala, Five Tribes builds on a long tradition of German-style games that feature wooden meeples. Here, in a unique twist on the now-standard \"worker placement\" genre, the game begins with the meeples already in place - and players must cleverly maneuver them over the villages, markets, oases, and sacred places tiles that make up Naqala. How, when, and where you dis-place these Five Tribes of Assassins, Elders, Builders, Merchants, and Viziers determine your victory or failure.",
    fogOfLove: "Fog of Love is a game for two players. You will create and play two vivid characters who meet, fall in love and face the challenge of making an unusual relationship work.",
    foodChainMagnate: "Food Chain Magnate is a heavy strategy game about building a fast food chain. The focus is on building your company using a card-driven (human) resource management system. Players compete on a variable city map through purchasing, marketing and sales, and on a job market for key staff members. The game can be played by 2-5 serious gamers in 2-4 hours.",
    forestShuffle: "In Forest Shuffle, players compete to gather the most valuable trees, then attract species to these trees, thus creating an ecologically balanced habitat for flora and fauna.",
    formaggio: "Formaggio is a simultaneous worker-placement game where players place Workers to make cheese and gather resources from the quadrant of the board facing them. Once all players have placed their Workers, the board rotates, aging any cheese that was made, and presenting each player with a new quadrant to place Workers into. Score Prestige Points by selling cheese to the four locations, and by efficiently managing and upgrading your creamery.",
    fromage: "Fromage is a simultaneous worker-placement game where players place Workers to make cheese and gather resources from the quadrant of the board facing them. Once all players have placed their Workers, the board rotates, aging any cheese that was made, and presenting each player with a new quadrant to place Workers into. Score Prestige Points by selling cheese to the four locations, and by efficiently managing and upgrading your creamery.",
    funemployed: "Funemployed is a card-based party game in which everyone's trying to become employed. Apply for real jobs, like astronaut, lawyer or priest, with unreal qualifications, such as a dragon, the ability to speak panda, or a DeLorean. In the game, each player uses their qualifications to convince the other players that they're the best qualified for a job. To do this, players tell the story of why their qualifications make them the best fit for a job by role-playing and acting like they are on an interview. Find innovative ways to use your qualifications and become the most \"funemployed\" player at the table!",
    furyOfDracula: "Fury of Dracula features art and graphic design crafted to complement the game's intuitive, thematic mechanisms. Rounds are broken into day and night, with hunters taking actions during both, while Dracula can act only at night. Combat is streamlined and decisive, and rumor tokens allow Dracula to mislead hunters and extend the terrible reach of his influence. Count Dracula triumphs if he advances his influence track to thirteen; if the hunters can defeat him before then, they save the continent of Europe and win the game.",
    fuse: "FUSE is a real-time co-operative game that employs 25 dice and 65 cards. Each game is set to a ten-minute timer, and players must work together in that ten minutes to defuse all of the bombs. Each bomb is represented by a card which needs a certain combination of dice in order to defuse it. A player will draw a number of dice equal to the number of players out of a bag and roll them. Players must then decide who will get which dice, but each player must take one and only one.",
    gameOfThrones: "In the second edition of A Game of Thrones: The Board Game, three to six players take on the roles of the great Houses of the Seven Kingdoms of Westeros, as they vie for control of the Iron Throne through the use of diplomacy and warfare. Based on the best-selling A Song of Ice and Fire series of fantasy novels by George R.R. Martin, A Game of Thrones is an epic board game in which it will take more than military might to win. Will you take power through force, use honeyed words to coerce your way onto the throne, or rally the townsfolk to your side? Through strategic planning, masterful diplomacy, and clever card play, spread your influence over Westeros!",
    go: "In Go, players alternately place stones on the empty intersections of a 19x19 grid. The goal: to enclose territory behind stone perimeters and, secondarily, to tightly surround and capture enemy stones. After both players pass, they add up their territory and deduct the number of captives lost, higher score wins.",
    gonutsForDonuts: "Go Nuts for Donuts is a fast-paced card game for the whole family with just a sprinkle of strategy. Outsmart your opponents and collect donuts hot out of the oven for points. But beware, if two players go after the same donut, then no one gets it!",
    grandAustriaHotel: "In the thick of the Viennese modern age, exquisite cafés are competing for customers. Inspiring artists, important politicians, and tourists from all over the world are populating Vienna and in need of a hotel room. This is your opportunity to turn your little café into a world famous hotel. Hire staff, fulfill the wishes of your guests, and gain the emperor's favor. Only then will your café become the Grand Austria Hotel.",
    gravwell: "In Gravwell, players command spaceships that have been pulled through a black hole, transporting them into a different dimension. With each ship lacking fuel to get home, each player must collect basic elements from surrounding asteroids, using the gravity of the dimension and what little resources they have in order to reach the warp gate that will take them home. But in this dimension, moving ships will travel towards the nearest object, which is usually another ship, and when those objects are moving either forward or backward, reaching the warp gate isn't always easy. Time is running out to save your crew and your ship! As a grim reminder of the cost of failing to escape, the frozen hulks of dead spacecraft litter the escape route — but with careful card play, you can slingshot past these derelict craft and be the first to escape from the Gravwell!",
    hanabi: "Hanabi—named for the Japanese word for \"fireworks\"—is a cooperative game in which players try to create the perfect fireworks show by placing the cards on the table in the right order. (In Japanese, hanabi is written as 花火; these are the ideograms flower and fire, respectively.)",
    harmonies: "In Harmonies, build landscapes by placing colored tokens and create habitats for your animals. To earn the most points and win the game, incorporate the habitats in your landscapes wisely and have as many animals as you can settle there.",
    heatPetalToTheMetal: "Based on simple and intuitive hand management, Heat: Pedal to the Metal puts players in the driver's seat of intense car races, jockeying for position to cross the finish line first, while managing their car's speed if they don't want to overheat. Selecting the right upgrades for their car will help them hug the curves and keep their engine cool enough to maintain top speeds. Ultimately, their driving skills will be the key to victory!",
    horizonsOfSpiritIsland: "Horizons of Spirit Island features the core mechanisms of Spirit Island, but features a new double-sided game board with a streamlined set-up, punchboard components, and five new Spirits designed to be ideal for those playing a Spirit Island game for the first time. These new Spirits are compatible with all existing Spirit Island components, but to play with expansions like Jagged Earth, you would need a copy of Spirit Island itself.",
    horselessCarriage: "Horseless Carriage is a game about the dawn of the automobile, a time when cars were invented, and no one quite knew yet what this new contraption would look like and what features would be essential. Early cars sometimes used levers or pedals to steer and a wheel to accelerate. Brakes were not always seen as essential, but sometimes an outside spot to take along an onboard mechanic was. This early, super innovative period occurs in the development of many new product categories. Players are cast as aspiring industrialists trying to find out what features the public will value when buying these new, expensive, and utterly unfamiliar horseless carriages.",
    hyperborea: "Set in a mythical land of the same name, Hyperborea is a heavy civilization game for 2 to 6 players that takes 20-25 minutes per player. The game begins at the time when the magic barrier protecting access to the mythical continent of Hyperborea suddenly falls.",
    iceCool: "ICECOOL is a flicking game in which each round one of the players takes the role of the Hall Monitor (also called \"the Catcher\") - his aim will be to catch each other penguin and get points for that. The others (also known as \"Runners\") will try to run through several doors, thus gaining fish (that give them points) on their way. When either the Hall Monitor has caught each other penguin once or any of the others has gone through all 3 doors that have fish on them, the round is over. Each player will take the role of the Hall Monitor once and at the end of the game the winner will be the one with the most points on their fish cards.",
    iceCool2: "ICECOOL2 is both a standalone game and an expansion for ICECOOL. If played on its own, ICECOOL2 differs from the original game.",
    incanGold: "Diamant — also published as Incan Gold — is a quick, fun, press-your-luck game. Players venture down mine shafts or explore paths in the jungle by turning up cards from a deck and evenly sharing the gems they find on the way, with any leftover gems being placed on the card. Before the next card is revealed, you have the chance to leave the mine and stash your holdings, including any gems you get on the way out.",
    irishGauge: "Diamant — also published as Incan Gold — is a quick, fun, press-your-luck game. Players venture down mine shafts or explore paths in the jungle by turning up cards from a deck and evenly sharing the gems they find on the way, with any leftover gems being placed on the card. Before the next card is revealed, you have the chance to leave the mine and stash your holdings, including any gems you get on the way out.",
    jenga: "Jenga is tower building game played with 54 wooden blocks; each block is 3 times as long as it is wide, and slightly smaller in height than in width. The blocks are stacked in a tower formation; each story is three blocks placed adjacent to each other along their long side, and each story is placed perpendicular to the previous (so, for example, if the blocks in the first story are pointing north-south, the second story blocks will point east-west). There are therefore 18 stories to the Jenga tower. Since stacking the blocks neatly can be tedious, a plastic loading tray is included.",
    jungleSpeed: "In Jungle Speed, you must rely on your keen sense of observation and quick reflexes. It requires a steady hand -- which can be hard to maintain during the many fits of maniacal laughter! The wooden Totem sits in the middle of the table, waiting for the player with the fastest reflexes to snatch it up and win the game.",
    justOne: "Just One is a co-operative party game in which you all play together to get the best score! Your goal each round is to get one player — the active player — to guess a mystery word based on the clues given by teammates. Can you achieve a perfect score by guessing all the mystery words?",
    keyFlower: "Keyflower is a game for two to six players played over four rounds. Each round represents a season: spring, summer, autumn, and finally winter. Each player starts the game with a \"home\" tile and an initial team of eight workers, each of which is colored red, yellow, or blue. Workers of matching colors are used by the players to bid for tiles to add to their villages. Matching workers may alternatively be used to generate resources, skills and additional workers, not only from the player's own tiles, but also from the tiles in the other players' villages and from the new tiles being auctioned.",
    keyFlowerTheMerchants: "In Keyflower: The Merchants, the second expansion for Keyflower, players continue to develop their village by building extensions and cabins, entering into lucrative contracts, and encountering new combinations of items on the incoming boats.",
    kingdomino: "In Kingdomino, you are a lord seeking new lands in which to expand your kingdom. You must explore all the lands, including wheat fields, lakes, and mountains, in order to spot the best plots, while competing with other lords to acquire them first.",
    kyoto: "Kyoto takes players straight into one of the burning issues of our time: climate change — and not with a wagging finger, but by putting them into the shoes of the decision makers.",
    lanterns: "In Lanterns: The Harvest Festival, players have a hand of tiles depicting various color arrangements of floating lanterns, as well as an inventory of individual lantern cards of specific colors. When you place a tile, all players (you and your opponents) receive a lantern card corresponding to the color on the side of the tile facing them. Place carefully to earn cards and other bonuses for yourself, while also looking to deny your opponents. Players gain honor by dedicating sets of lantern cards — three pairs, for example, or all seven colors — and the player with the most honor at the end of the game wins.",
    leHavre: "In Le Havre, a player's turn consists of two parts: First, distribute newly supplied goods onto the offer spaces; then take an action. As an action, players may choose either to take all goods of one type from an offer space or to use one of the available buildings. Building actions allow players to upgrade goods, sell them or use them to build their own buildings and ships. Buildings are both an investment opportunity and a revenue stream, as players must pay an entry fee to use buildings that they do not own. Ships, on the other hand, are primarily used to provide the food that is needed to feed the workers.",
    lemonadeStand: "Lemonade Stand is played over seven turns (days), and each turn players start by turning over a forecast card which shows the weather forecast for the day along with number of customers and the price they will be willing to pay for each possible weather outcome. Players then place a 5, 10 or 15 cent price card down along with any signs or lemonade inventory they want to put out, all face down. All players reveal their cards at the same time and then a new forecast card is revealed which has an arrow pointing to one of five spots on the old forecast card, which determines which weather event occurred. Each player then collects money based on their price and # of glasses of lemonade invested versus the actual weather that happened.",
    letterJam: "Letter Jam is a 2-6 player cooperative word game where players assist each other in composing meaningful words from letters around the table. The trick is holding the letter card so that it’s only visible to other players and not to you.",
    lettersFromWhitechapel: "One player plays Jack the Ripper, and his goal is to take five victims before being caught. The other players are police detectives who must cooperate to catch Jack the Ripper before the end of the game. The game board represents the Whitechapel area at the time of Jack the Ripper and is marked with 199 numbered circles linked together by dotted lines. During play, Jack the Ripper, the Policemen, and the Wretched are moved along the dotted lines that represent Whitechapel's streets. Jack the Ripper moves stealthily between numbered circles, while policemen move on their patrols between crossings, and the Wretched wander alone between the numbered circles.",
    

    spiritIsland: "Spirit Island is a complex and thematic co-operative game about defending your island home from colonizing Invaders. Players are different spirits of the land, each with its own unique elemental powers. Every turn, players simultaneously choose which of their power cards to play, paying energy to do so. Using combinations of power cards that match a spirit's elemental affinities can grant free bonus effects. Faster powers take effect immediately, before the Invaders spread and ravage, but other magics are slower, requiring forethought and planning to use effectively. In the Spirit phase, spirits gain energy, and choose how / whether to Grow: to reclaim used power cards, to seek new power, or to spread their presence into new areas of the island.",

    slayTheSpire: "Slay the Spire: The Board Game is a co-operative deck-building, dungeon-crawling adventure. Craft a unique deck, encounter bizarre creatures, discover relics of immense power, and finally become strong enough to slay the Spire!",

    liarsDice: "Liar's Dice is a classic bluffing game in which each player has five dice hidden under a cup. Players bid on how many of a certain number appear among all dice in play. Each successive bid must be higher than the last. Players can call the previous bidder a liar, at which point all cups are lifted and the dice are counted. The loser must give up one of their dice, and the player who keeps dice the longest wins.",
    libertalia: "In Libertalia, players are pirates fighting over treasure. Each player has an identical set of crew cards, and each round they secretly pick one card to play simultaneously. Cards are revealed, resolved in order of their rank, and loot is divided. Over three rounds, players build up their crew and compete to amass the most gold. The twist is that everyone has the same cards, so outthinking your opponents is key.",
    lostCities: "Lost Cities is a card game of risk and reward in which players mount archaeological expeditions to five mysterious locations. Each expedition track requires a significant investment, but expeditions that fall short of 20 points cost you. Careful timing and hand management are essential to outscore your opponent in this elegant two-player game.",
    lostRuinsOfArnak: "Lost Ruins of Arnak combines deck building with worker placement on a unique, thematic map. Players lead an expedition exploring a newly discovered island. Overcome guardians of ancient sites, acquire artifacts and research, and advance along the research track to uncover the mysteries of Arnak. The mix of deck building and worker placement creates a dynamic, variable experience every time you play.",
    loveLetter: "Love Letter: Princess Princess Ever After is a quick, accessible card game in which players compete to deliver their letter to the princess. With only 16 cards in the deck, each turn you draw one card and play one card, using character abilities to outmaneuver your opponents and ensure your love letter reaches its destination.",
    machiKoro: "In Machi Koro, you are the mayor of a fledgling city and your goal is to be the first to construct all of the city's landmark buildings. On your turn, roll the dice and collect income from your establishments, then spend those coins to build new establishments or fund your landmarks. Cleverly build your city, speculate on your opponents' dice rolls, and be the first to complete all four landmarks.",
    mageKnight: "Mage Knight Board Game puts you in the role of one of four powerful Mage Knights as you explore and conquer a corner of the Mage Knight universe. Build your armies, learn powerful spells, and conquer cities and dungeons in this epic solo or cooperative adventure. With a deep deck-building system and dense strategic decision-making, Mage Knight is one of the most complex and rewarding games in the genre.",
    mansionsOfMadness: "Mansions of Madness is a fully cooperative, app-driven game of mystery and investigation inspired by the works of H.P. Lovecraft. One to five players explore a haunted mansion, gather clues, solve puzzles, and battle terrifying monsters. The app handles all monsters, environment, and storytelling, creating an immersive narrative-driven experience that changes with every game.",
    medici: "Medici is a classic auction and trading game set in Renaissance Florence. Players bid on goods to fill their ships and sell commodities in the market. The player who controls the most valuable goods in each commodity at the end of each round earns points. A reprint of Reiner Knizia's acclaimed economic game, Medici rewards shrewd bidding and market manipulation.",
    memoir44: "Memoir '44 is a historical board game in which players re-create famous WWII battles using dice, cards, and miniatures. Each scenario is based on a real battle, and players command infantry, tanks, and artillery to outmaneuver the enemy. The Command and Colors system makes rules approachable while capturing the tension of battlefield decisions, from D-Day landings to the Pacific theater.",
    mentalBlocks: "Mental Blocks is a cooperative 3D spatial puzzle game in which each player holds a card showing part of a structure but can only see their own card. Working together, players must build the shape shown on the challenge card without directly showing each other their perspectives. Communication and spatial reasoning are key to solving the puzzle.",
    miceAndMystics: "Mice and Mystics is a cooperative, story-driven adventure game in which players take on the roles of heroes who have been transformed into mice. Together they navigate through chapters of an unfolding tale, battling rats, centipedes, and cockroaches while searching for the cure to restore them. The game features a campaign structure with persistent characters and a charming storybook narrative.",
    modernArt: "Modern Art is a classic auction game by Reiner Knizia in which players act as both art dealers and museum curators. Each round, players sell artworks by five artists using various auction formats. At the end of each round, the most popular artists are valued and players collect profits from their sales. The player with the most money wins.",
    monopolyCheatersEdition: "Monopoly: Cheater's Edition puts a twist on the classic board game by officially encouraging players to cheat. A set of cheat cards instructs players to secretly break the rules — collect extra money, avoid paying rent, or steal from other players. Get caught and you'll be handcuffed to the board; succeed and reap the rewards.",
    monopolyScoobyDoo: "Monopoly: Scooby-Doo Edition is a themed version of the classic Monopoly game featuring properties, tokens, and cards based on the beloved animated series. Players buy, sell, and trade Scooby-Doo locations and characters while navigating Chance and Community Chest cards styled after the gang's misadventures.",
    myFathersWork: "My Father's Work is a legacy-style game in which players become members of a family of brilliant, obsessive inventors across three generations. Each generation reveals new secrets about the family's dark history and mysterious experiments. Players manage workers, gather resources, and conduct bizarre research in a narrative-driven experience that permanently changes between playthroughs.",
    mysterium: "Mysterium is a cooperative deduction game in which one player is the ghost of a murdered victim, communicating with the other players through vivid dreamlike vision cards. The investigators must interpret the ghost's cryptic clues to identify the correct suspect, location, and weapon. With stunning artwork and a unique asymmetric communication system, Mysterium creates a truly atmospheric experience.",
    mysticPaths: "Mystic Paths is a tile-placement and route-building game in which players weave paths of magical energy across a shared board. By connecting nodes of matching colors, players score points and trigger special abilities. With limited actions each turn and a board that evolves as paths are built, Mystic Paths rewards careful planning and spatial awareness.",
    nertz: "Nertz is a fast-paced, real-time competitive card game played with a standard deck of cards. Players race simultaneously to play cards onto shared foundation piles in the center of the table, building up from Ace to King by suit. The first player to exhaust their Nertz pile calls 'Nertz!' and the round ends. Quick reflexes and sharp eyes are essential.",
    noThanks: "No Thanks! is a deceptively simple card game in which players try to avoid collecting high-value cards while desperately trying not to run out of chips. On your turn, you either take the face-up card and all chips on it, or you pay one chip to pass. Cards form sequential runs and only the lowest card in a run scores against you. The tension between greed and avoidance makes every decision agonizing.",
    oceans: "Oceans is an engine-building game set in the deep sea, where players evolve species and adapt them to a complex, dynamic ecosystem. Species feed, grow, and compete for food in the shallows, but the mysterious deep ocean holds powerful traits that can shift the game dramatically. With stunning artwork and modular depth, Oceans offers a rich and evolving tableau-building experience.",
    oneNightUltimateWerewolf: "One Night Ultimate Werewolf is a fast-paced social deduction game in which each player is secretly assigned a role — villager, werewolf, or special character. During a short night phase players close their eyes and some secretly swap roles. At dawn, players have just a few minutes to debate and vote on who to eliminate. With no moderator and games lasting under 10 minutes, it's perfect for large groups.",
    pandemicIberia: "Pandemic Iberia is a historical reimagining of the classic Pandemic set in the Iberian Peninsula in 1848. Players take on roles inspired by the 19th century and must stop four diseases from spreading across the region. New mechanics include purifying diseases by building hospitals and constructing railways to move more efficiently across the map.",
    pandemicOnTheBrink: "Pandemic: On the Brink is an expansion for the cooperative classic Pandemic that adds new roles, new events, and new challenges. The centerpiece includes a bio-terrorist who actively works against the team, a virulent strain that spreads faster, and a mutation of an existing disease. It also adds petri dish components for tracking mutations.",
    paranormalDetectives: "Paranormal Detectives is a deduction party game in which one player is a ghost and the others are detective investigators. The ghost cannot speak, but communicates through ghostly methods — Ouija boards, drawings, mime, and touch — to help detectives determine how they died. Players race to deduce the correct answer before the others. Creative and funny in equal measure.",
    parks: "PARKS is a celebration of America's national parks in which players take turns hiking trails and collecting memories of flora, fauna, and scenic beauty. Trade in your memories to visit parks and earn points. Each season the trail changes and grows more competitive. With gorgeous artwork from the Fifty-Nine Parks Print Series, PARKS is a visually stunning experience.",
    patchwork: "Patchwork is a two-player game of quilting and button economy. Players take turns buying oddly-shaped patches from a circular market to fill their personal 9x9 quilt board. Each patch costs time and buttons, and players earn more buttons as they sew patches with button icons. At the end of the game, empty spaces cost points. A perfectly crafted two-player puzzle.",
    pennyPress: "Penny Press is a press-your-luck and set-collection game set in the Golden Age of newspaper publishing. Players are rival editors competing to scoop the best stories and print the most compelling edition. Roll dice to gather news stories, manage your printing resources, and claim headlines before your opponents. Charming artwork makes Penny Press an accessible and enjoyable family experience.",
    planes: "Planes is a quick and charming abstract game in which players collect and organize sets of plane ticket cards. Players draft ticket cards of different colors and try to complete sets representing flights. With simple rules and a family-friendly theme, Planes is an easy entry into the world of set-collection card games.",
    planet: "Planet is a tile-drafting game in which players build three-dimensional magnetic planets, placing hexagonal terrain tiles to create the most hospitable habitats for animals. Each round, a new animal card is revealed that prefers a specific combination of terrains; whoever has the most of those terrains earns the card and its points. A beautiful, tactile game that doubles as table art.",
    potionExplosion: "Potion Explosion is a puzzle game in which players pull ingredients out of a marble dispenser and trigger chain reactions of matching marbles. The ingredients collected are used to brew potions that grant special abilities and victory points. With a satisfying physical component and a constant push for the perfect combo, Potion Explosion is a clever and tactile puzzle game.",
    powerGrid: "Power Grid is a strategic network-building game in which players compete to supply electricity to the most cities. Players bid on power plants at auction, buy resources to fuel them, and expand their network across the map. Market prices for resources fluctuate based on demand, and the player who powers the most cities wins. A masterwork of economic tension and turn-order manipulation.",
    puertoRico: "Puerto Rico is a classic role-selection strategy game set on the island of Puerto Rico during the colonial era. Players choose from roles like Settler, Builder, Mayor, and Trader to develop their plantations, construct buildings, and ship goods to Europe. Each role benefits all players slightly, but the active player gains the most. A landmark of modern game design with deep strategic decisions.",
    quoridor: "Quoridor is an abstract strategy game in which each player moves their pawn toward the opposite side of the board while placing wooden fences to block opponents. Players must always leave a path open, turning the game into a battle of spatial reasoning and anticipation. Simple to learn but deeply strategic, Quoridor is a modern classic of abstract design.",
    raidersOfTheNorthSea: "Raiders of the North Sea is a worker-placement game set in a Viking-age world. Players assemble a crew of powerful warriors, gather provisions and plunder, and lead raids on distant settlements. The central mechanic — placing a colored worker to take an action, then picking up a different worker to unlock another — creates a dynamic push-and-pull that keeps every turn interesting.",
    railroadInk: "Railroad Ink Challenge is a roll-and-write game in which players draw roads and railways on individual boards based on dice results. Connecting exits scores points, while isolated networks earn penalties. Each edition features a different challenge expansion that adds a unique twist. A satisfying solo or simultaneous-play puzzle.",
    railwaysOfTheWorld: "Railways of the World is an epic train game in which players compete to build the most extensive and profitable railway network. Players deliver goods between cities, upgrade their locomotives, and compete for lucrative railway bonds. With beautiful components, an economic engine that rewards long-term planning, and multiple maps, Railways of the World is a definitive train game experience.",
    raiseYourGoblets: "Raise Your Goblets is a bluffing and social deduction game set at a Renaissance banquet. Players secretly add wine and poison to goblets around the table — including their own. At the end of the round, everyone drinks. Clever use of peek, swap, and empty actions makes every round a delightful game of misdirection and survival.",
    redRising: "Red Rising is a hand-management and tableau-building card game based on Pierce Brown's science fiction novel series. Players draft cards from a central market and play them to their faction tableau, triggering powerful abilities and collecting leaders. The economy of cards — knowing when to play them, when to save them, and how to exploit your opponents — drives deep replayability.",
    rollForTheGalaxy: "Roll for the Galaxy is a dice-based civilization-building game in which players command space empires and use dice representing their population to develop planets, research technologies, and ship goods. Each player selects a tile secretly, and the dice phase is simultaneous — but only players who chose the matching tile get the full benefit. A clever race to build the most powerful galactic civilization.",
    root: "Root is a game of adventure and war in which players battle for control of a vast wilderness. Each player controls a unique faction with completely different rules and goals — the Marquise de Cat builds industries, the Eyrie Dynasties execute strict decrees, the Woodland Alliance foments a revolution, and the Vagabond roams freely. The asymmetry creates a dynamic and deeply strategic conflict unlike any other.",
    rootMarauder: "Root: The Marauder Expansion adds two new factions and the Hirelings system to Root. The Keepers in Iron defend ancient relics, while the Lord of the Hundreds commands a horde of rats. Hirelings are small neutral parties that players can recruit and use to exert influence across the board, adding a new layer of interaction.",
    rootRiverfolk: "Root: The Riverfolk Expansion adds two new factions to Root — the Riverfolk Company, a mercenary trading faction that sells services to other factions, and the Lizard Cult, a religious faction that converts lost warriors into adherents. It also introduces the Mechanical Marquise 2.0, an updated automated faction for solo and cooperative play.",
    rootUnderworld: "Root: The Underworld Expansion introduces two new factions and two new maps. The Underground Duchy rules from below through a noble senate, while the Corvid Conspiracy uses plots and deception to spread across the board. The two new maps — the mountain map and the lake map — add new traversal mechanics and strategic variety.",
    saboteur: "Saboteur is a hidden role card game set in a dwarf gold mine. Most players are gold-digger dwarves trying to build a tunnel from start to goal, while one or more saboteurs secretly work to block their progress. Players play tunnel cards or action cards each turn, and it's up to the dwarves to figure out who among them is the saboteur before they ruin the path to the gold.",
    sagrada: "Sagrada is a dice-drafting puzzle game in which players are master artisans competing to craft the most beautiful stained glass windows of the Sagrada Familia. Each round players draft colorful dice and place them on their window pattern cards following color and shade restrictions. Tools help bend the rules, and public and private objectives guide where points come from. A visual and strategic gem.",
    santorini: "Santorini is a pure strategy game inspired by the beautiful Greek island. Players take turns moving their builders and constructing buildings across a three-dimensional board. The first player to move their builder to the third level of a building wins. The elegant base game is enriched by a pantheon of god cards that grant special powers, creating enormous variety.",
    scoobyDooBetrayal: "Scooby-Doo! Betrayal at Mystery Mansion is a kid-friendly version of Betrayal at House on the Hill featuring the Scooby-Doo cast. Players explore a haunted mansion together until one player secretly becomes the villain and must complete an evil scheme while the others work to stop them. A gentle introduction to the hidden traitor genre.",
    scoobyDooHideAndShriek: "Scooby-Doo! Hide and Shriek Game is a family ghost-hunting game set in a spooky mansion. Players cooperatively search for clues and avoid the ghost while trying to unmask the villain before time runs out. Designed for younger audiences with accessible rules and colorful Scooby-Doo artwork.",
    scoobyDooThrills: "Scooby-Doo! Thrills and Spills Game is a family-friendly racing and adventure game featuring the Scooby-Doo gang. Players race to collect clues and solve the mystery before their opponents. With simple mechanics and a beloved license, it's designed to bring fans of the animated series to the table.",
    scout: "Scout is a quick and clever card game in which players have a hand of cards they cannot rearrange. On your turn, you can either play a valid set of cards from your hand to the table, or Scout — take up to two cards from the table to insert into your hand in any position. The trick is that you can never reorder your hand. A brilliant puzzle of positioning and timing.",
    scoville: "Scoville is a worker-placement game centered on the competitive breeding of chili peppers. Players plant, harvest, and cross-breed peppers to create increasingly hot varieties, then sell them at market and complete recipe orders. The unique pepper-crossing mechanic, in which peppers in adjacent plots combine to create new species, gives the game a satisfying agricultural puzzle.",
    set: "Set is a real-time card game of visual perception in which players race to find valid sets among a grid of cards. Each card has four properties — color, shape, number, and shading — and a set consists of three cards where each property is either all the same or all different across the three cards. Fast, stimulating, and endlessly replayable.",
    shadowsOverCamelot: "Shadows Over Camelot is a cooperative game set in the world of Arthurian legend. Players are Knights of the Round Table working together to complete quests and defend Camelot. However, one of the knights may secretly be a traitor working to undermine the group. Balancing trust and suspicion while completing quests makes every game a dramatic story.",
    sheriffOfNottingham: "Sheriff of Nottingham is a bluffing and negotiation game in which players attempt to sneak contraband goods past the Sheriff. Each round, players pack goods into a bag, declare what's inside, and try to bribe or convince the Sheriff to let it pass. Inspect a bag and you're wrong? You pay a penalty. Lies, deals, and betrayals make every round memorable.",
    shogi: "Shogi is the traditional Japanese form of chess, played on a 9x9 board with 20 pieces per player. What distinguishes Shogi from Western chess is the drop rule — captured pieces join your own army and can be re-entered anywhere on the board on future turns. This creates complex tactical positions and an explosive late game unlike any Western chess variant.",
    skull: "Skull is an ultra-simple bluffing game in which each player places flowers or skulls face-down in a stack. Players then bid on how many flowers they can flip without hitting a skull. The highest bidder must flip their own stack first, then others. Two wins earns victory. Elegant, tense, and endlessly readable.",
    smallworld: "Small World is a fantasy area-control game in which players pick up and discard fantasy races — each combined with a random special power — to conquer territories and score points. When a race becomes too spread out, players put it into decline and start fresh with a new combination. With 14 races and 20 special powers, no two games play the same.",
    smallworldUnderground: "Small World Underground is a standalone companion to Small World set in a fantastical underground world. New races like the Were-Moles and Cthonians battle for territories through caverns, lakes, and ancient ruins. It features the same pick-up-and-discard race drafting system with a new set of underground-themed races and powers.",
    snollygoster: "Snollygoster is a political bluffing card game in which players act as candidates running for President. Play issue cards, make promises you may not keep, and manipulate the election to your advantage. With a satirical take on campaign politics and fast, chaotic gameplay, Snollygoster is a humorous look at what it takes to win an election.",
    soClover: "So Clover! is a cooperative word game in which each player privately arranges four keyword cards on a clover-shaped board and writes one clue for each pair of adjacent keywords. Then the group works together to reconstruct who wrote which clue and how the keywords were originally arranged. A warm, clever twist on word association that shines at any table.",
    specterOps: "Specter Ops is a hidden-movement game of cat and mouse in which one player is a covert agent infiltrating a secret facility, while the other players are hunters tracking them down. The agent moves secretly on their own paper map while the hunters try to deduce their location and cut them off. Tense, tactical, and perfectly asymmetric.",
    spiritIslandFeatherAndFlame: "Spirit Island: Feather and Flame is an expansion for Spirit Island adding two new Spirits — Starlight Seeks Its Form and Ember-Eyed Behemoth — along with new adversaries, scenarios, and Dahan leaders with unique abilities. The expansion deepens the narrative and mechanical complexity of the base game.",
    spiritIslandJaggedEarth: "Spirit Island: Jagged Earth is the largest expansion for Spirit Island, adding ten new Spirits, two new Adversaries, new scenarios, and new Event cards that make the island feel more dynamic. It introduces Strife tokens and Elemental Thresholds, and the new Spirits cover a wide range of playstyles from aggressive to subtly defensive.",
    splendor: "Splendor is an elegant gem-collecting and card-development game in which players are Renaissance merchants acquiring gem mines, transportation routes, and shops. Each turn, players collect gem tokens or buy development cards that provide permanent gems and victory points. Be the first to reach 15 prestige points to win. Simple to learn, rich to master, and endlessly satisfying.",
    spyfall: "Spyfall is a social deduction party game in which all players except one know the location of a secret meeting. The odd one out is the Spy, who must figure out the location by listening to players' coded answers to questions. Meanwhile, the other players try to identify the Spy without giving too much away. Fast, funny, and unpredictable.",
    stardewValley: "Stardew Valley: The Board Game is a cooperative game based on the beloved farming video game. Players work together to restore the Community Center, befriend the villagers, and grow their farm before the seasons end. With farm upgrades, foraging, fishing, and mining, the board game faithfully captures the charm and progression of the original game.",
    starWarsRebellion: "Star Wars: Rebellion is an epic two-player game set in the Galactic Civil War. One player commands the Galactic Empire, trying to crush the Rebellion and find its secret base; the other leads the Rebel Alliance, striking at key targets while hiding their base. With iconic characters, massive fleets, and cinematic narrative play, it's one of the most immersive thematic games ever made.",
    subdivision: "Subdivision is a tile-laying game in which players develop suburban neighborhoods, placing streets, parks, schools, and homes on their personal grids. Points are scored by building adjacencies and completing criteria tied to city services. With tight decisions and a clever scoring system, Subdivision is a satisfying puzzle.",
    suburbia: "Suburbia is a tile-laying city-building game in which players develop a personal borough by purchasing hexagonal building tiles and arranging them to maximize population growth and income. As your borough grows, buildings interact in surprising ways, boosting or reducing income and population. The player with the most population at game end wins.",
    sushiGo: "Sushi Go! is a fast and adorable card-drafting game in which players pass hands of sushi cards around the table, keeping one card each turn. Collect the most maki rolls, complete sets of sashimi, or stack dumplings for big points. With simple rules and charming artwork, Sushi Go! is a perfect introduction to drafting games.",
    sushiGoParty: "Sushi Go Party! is an expanded version of Sushi Go! featuring a party board and a much larger selection of sushi cards. Before each game, players choose which cards to include from dozens of options, creating a customizable drafting experience. With more players, more variety, and the same charming artwork, Sushi Go Party! is the definitive edition for groups.",
    scythe: "Scythe is an engine-building game set in an alternate-history 1920s Europe where giant mechs roam the countryside. Players control factions with asymmetric abilities, deploying workers, building structures, and enrolling mechs to control territories and resources. The innovative action-selection system prevents players from taking the same action twice in a row. A stunning combination of theme, strategy, and art.",
    takenoko: "Takenoko is a charming strategy game in which players tend a bamboo garden gifted to the Emperor of Japan by a giant panda. Players draw and complete objective cards by growing bamboo, irrigating plots, and keeping the panda satisfied. With beautiful components, simple rules, and a delightful theme, Takenoko is a beloved family and gateway game.",
    terraformingMars: "Terraforming Mars is an epic engine-building game in which corporations compete to terraform the Red Planet by raising the temperature, oxygen level, and ocean coverage. Players play project cards, place tiles, and manage resources across a shared Martian board. With hundreds of unique project cards and asymmetric starting corporations, every game tells a different story of humanity's colonization of Mars.",
    terraformingMarsAresExpedition: "Terraforming Mars: Ares Expedition distills the full Terraforming Mars experience into a faster card game format. Players simultaneously select one of five phases each round, and only the selected phases occur. Build your engine, manage resources, and terraform Mars in 60 to 90 minutes. A streamlined and highly replayable take on the beloved original.",
    terraformingMarsColonies: "Terraforming Mars: Colonies is an expansion that takes players beyond the Red Planet. Players can now build colonies on the moons of the outer solar system, opening up new trading routes and earning powerful bonuses. New cards interact with the colony system, adding a new layer of strategy without significantly increasing game length.",
    terraMystica: "Terra Mystica is a deep strategy game in which 14 factions of fantasy creatures compete to terraform the landscape to their preferred terrain type and build structures across a shared board. Each faction has unique abilities and powers that develop over the course of the game. With tight resource management, complex action planning, and little luck, Terra Mystica is one of the most celebrated heavy games.",
    terrorBelow: "Terror Below is a B-movie-inspired game of government experiments gone wrong in the Nevada desert. Players race across the board collecting worm eggs while avoiding a massive lurking worm that hunts by sound. Deliver eggs to lucrative locations for points, but disturb too many spaces and the worm comes for you. Fast, tense, and dripping with campy charm.",
    terrorBelowHiddenCache: "Terror Below: Hidden Cache is an expansion for Terror Below that introduces new worm cards, new locations, new government experiments, and relic tokens hidden across the board. The expansion adds depth and variability to the base game with new ways to score and new dangers lurking underground.",
    terrorInMeepleCity: "Terror in Meeple City is a dexterity game in which giant monsters rampage through a cardboard city. Players physically flick their monster discs across the board, trying to knock over building stacks and gobble up the little meeples inside. Pure chaotic fun for groups who enjoy physical dexterity games with a humorous theme.",
    theArrival: "The Arrival is a competitive strategy game set in ancient Celtic mythology, in which players lead clans encroaching on the mystical island of Tir na nOg. Players spread across the land, build sacred sites, and gain the favor of gods — but the Fomorians, dark creatures of the island, push back against unchecked expansion. Pollute the land too much and the Fomorians swarm.",
    theCrewMissionDeepSea: "The Crew: Mission Deep Sea is a cooperative trick-taking card game in which players work together to complete a series of increasingly difficult missions. Each mission assigns specific tasks — a player must win a certain card, or must win a trick before another player — and success requires careful communication under strict rules. A brilliant reimagining of trick-taking as a collaborative puzzle.",
    theFoxInTheForest: "The Fox in the Forest is an elegant trick-taking game for exactly two players. Cards feature fairy-tale creatures with unique abilities that allow you to change the trump suit, swap cards with the deck, or force your opponent to lead. Score too many tricks and you become greedy, losing points instead of earning them. A beautifully balanced two-player card game.",
    theIsleOfCats: "The Isle of Cats is a competitive tile-drafting and puzzle game in which players are explorers rescuing cats from a mythical island. Players draft lesson and cat cards, then fill their boat with polyomino-shaped cat tiles, trying to complete families and minimize gaps. The combination of drafting and placement puzzles is deeply satisfying.",
    theQuacksOfQuedlinburg: "The Quacks of Quedlinburg is a push-your-luck bag-building game in which players are quack doctors brewing potions by drawing ingredients from their bags. Keep drawing for more powerful potions, but pull too many white chips and your pot explodes. Between rounds, players buy new ingredient chips to improve their bags. Chaotic, tense, and endlessly entertaining.",
    theRepublicOfRome: "The Republic of Rome is a monumental political strategy game simulating the internal power struggles and external threats facing the Roman Senate. Players control senatorial families competing for power while collectively managing Rome's legions, economy, and crises. Semi-cooperative and cutthroat, it is one of the most ambitious political simulations in board gaming.",
    theResistance: "The Resistance is a social deduction party game in which a team of rebels fights against an empire. Most players are rebels, but a few are imperial spies. Each round, a leader proposes a mission team and players vote to approve or reject it. On approved missions, team members secretly pass or fail. The rebels win if three missions succeed; the empire wins if three fail.",
    theSearchForPlanetX: "The Search for Planet X is a deduction game in which players are astronomers searching for a hidden celestial body. Using a companion app to survey sectors of the sky, players gather clues about the positions of comets, asteroids, and dwarf planets to logically deduce Planet X's exact location. A satisfying scientific puzzle with elegant deductive mechanics.",
    theTeaDragonSociety: "The Tea Dragon Society Card Game is a gentle, cooperative game based on the graphic novel by Katie O'Neill. Players guide tea dragons through the seasons, growing plants and brewing teas to create memories. With soothing artwork and accessible mechanics, The Tea Dragon Society is a warm and welcoming game for players of all ages.",
    ticketToRide: "Ticket to Ride is the beloved classic in which players collect sets of colored train cards and use them to claim railway routes across North America. Complete your secret destination tickets — connecting distant cities — for bonus points, but watch out for opponents who might block your paths. Simple to learn and deeply satisfying, Ticket to Ride is the ideal gateway game.",
    ticketToRideUK: "Ticket to Ride: United Kingdom challenges players to build railway networks across Britain and Ireland while developing locomotive technology. Unlike the base game, players must research progressively advanced technologies before they can lay certain routes. A richer, more complex Ticket to Ride experience with a beautifully illustrated Victorian map.",
    tigrisAndEuphrates: "Tigris and Euphrates is Reiner Knizia's acclaimed civilization-building game set in the ancient Fertile Crescent. Players place tiles representing leaders, traders, farmers, and priests to build kingdoms and trigger conflicts. Your score is determined by your weakest civilization type — a brilliant balancing mechanism that forces players to develop all aspects of their civilization equally.",
    timeStories: "TIME Stories is a cooperative narrative adventure game in which players are time agents sent back in time to correct anomalies. Players explore illustrated cards depicting different locations in a historical setting, gathering clues and making decisions that unfold a branching story. Designed as a series of scenarios, each adventure is a single-use mystery to be solved.",
    tomorrow: "Tomorrow is a light, quick card game in which players compete to complete tasks and earn points. With simple mechanics and accessible gameplay, Tomorrow is a great filler for gaming groups looking for a fast and fun experience between heavier games.",
    trains: "Trains is a deck-building game set in Japan in which players are railroad companies laying tracks and building stations across the board. Buying cards builds your deck, while playing route cards builds the actual railway network on the physical board. Waste cards accumulate in your deck from expanding into occupied areas, creating a resource management tension unique in the deck-building genre.",
    trajan: "Trajan is a complex strategy game by Stefan Feld in which players are Roman senators competing for influence during the reign of Emperor Trajan. A unique mancala-style action selection mechanism drives the game, requiring players to plan several turns ahead to unlock powerful actions. Multiple scoring paths — military, trade, forum, and construction — create a rich optimization puzzle.",
    trickerion: "Trickerion is a worker-placement game set in a dark 1920s fantasy city where players are rival magicians competing for fame and fortune. Players send their magician, assistant, and apprentice to different locations to acquire tricks, gather components, and perform spectacular illusions. With a deep action economy and large variety of tricks, Trickerion rewards long-term planning.",
    tsukuyumi: "Tsukuyumi: Full Moon Down is an asymmetric area-control game set in a mythic alternate-future Japan where the moon has crashed into Earth. Players control unique factions — ancient Japanese spirits and modern military forces — battling for the shattered moon's territory. Each faction has radically different rules and strategies, making every matchup feel like a completely different game.",
    tuscanyEssentialEdition: "Tuscany Essential Edition is an expansion for Viticulture that transforms it into a richer game. It introduces a new board with a seasonal action-space structure, worker placement areas that open up over time, and a new trade mechanic. The Essential Edition compiles the best components from the original Tuscany expansion into a focused package.",
    twilightImperium: "Twilight Imperium is a legendary space opera board game of galactic conquest, politics, and trade. Three to six players command unique alien civilizations competing to claim the throne of the galaxy. Fleets clash in epic space battles, political agendas reshape the galaxy's laws, and secret objectives reward cunning and deception. One of the most ambitious and immersive tabletop experiences ever created.",
    twilightImperiumRex: "Twilight Imperium: Rex — Final Days of an Empire is a game of negotiation, betrayal, and tactical conflict set in the twilight of a galactic empire. Players control unique alien factions competing to capture Mecatol City before it falls. Combining a politics and alliance system with combat, Rex delivers a tense experience for three to six players.",
    twilightInscription: "Twilight Inscription is a roll-and-write game set in the Twilight Imperium universe in which players chart the rise of their space empires on individual sheets. Each round, dice are drafted and used to expand territory, advance technology, and score political agendas. With four interlocking sheets per player and faction-specific abilities, Twilight Inscription packs remarkable depth into the roll-and-write format.",
    twoRoomsAndABoom: "Two Rooms and a Boom is a large-group social deduction game in which players are split into two rooms and belong to secret teams. The Blue Team protects the President; the Red Team wants to put the Bomber in the same room as the President at game end. Players negotiate, trade hostages, and deduce identities across three timed rounds. Best with 10 to 30 people.",
    tzolkin: "Tzolk'in: The Mayan Calendar is a worker-placement game with an extraordinary central mechanic — workers are placed on interlocking gears that rotate each round. Placing workers is free, but retrieving them costs corn. Time your placements perfectly to collect maximum rewards from the rotating gears while feeding your workers and advancing your civilization.",
    underwaterCities: "Underwater Cities is a complex worker-placement and network-building game in which players develop networks of underwater cities connected by tunnels on a shared board. Buildings — labs, farms, and desalination plants — improve the productivity of your network, and powerful action cards provide additional benefits. A deeply satisfying engine-builder that rewards careful long-term planning.",
    underwaterCitiesNewDiscoveries: "Underwater Cities: New Discoveries is an expansion for Underwater Cities that adds new buildings, metropolises, and personal player boards with unique faction abilities. New era cards add narrative flavor and new mechanics including research tracks. The expansion deepens the base game without significantly increasing complexity.",
    unfair: "Unfair is a theme-park building game in which players construct their own amusement parks while playing nasty event cards to sabotage their opponents. Upgrade your rides to maximize income and visitors, but expect your rivals to send disasters, thieves, and accidents your way. Chaotic and take-that in nature, Unfair leans into the sabotage theme with a colorful cartoonish style.",
    unlock: "Unlock! is a series of cooperative escape-room card games in which players have one hour to solve a mystery using a companion app. Cards represent locations, objects, and codes; combine numbered cards to discover new items and unlock new areas. A shared puzzle for everyone at the table that is affordable, portable, and single-use by design.",
    unlockANosideStory: "Unlock! Secret Adventures: A Noside Story is a standalone escape-room scenario in which players must stop the villainous Noside from enacting a devious plan. Using the Unlock! companion app and card-combination mechanic, players work cooperatively to find clues, solve codes, and unravel the mystery within 60 minutes.",
    unlockAdventuresOfOz: "Unlock! Secret Adventures: The Adventures of Oz is a standalone escape-room scenario that sends players to the magical land of Oz. Using the Unlock! companion app, players combine location and object cards to progress through Dorothy's adventure, solving puzzles and uncovering the path back home.",
    uno: "Uno is a classic shedding card game in which players race to empty their hands by matching the top card of the discard pile by color or number. Special action cards — Skip, Reverse, Draw Two, and the Wild Draw Four — add chaos and strategy. When you're down to your last card, shout Uno! or draw a penalty. A timeless game for all ages.",
    vastTheCrystalCaverns: "Vast: The Crystal Caverns is a wildly asymmetric dungeon-crawl game in which each player controls a completely different character with unique rules and victory conditions. The Knight hunts the Dragon, the Dragon sleeps and destroys, the Goblins swarm, the Thief loots the cave, and the Cave itself collapses around them. No two roles play alike.",
    villainous: "Disney Villainous is an asymmetric strategy game in which each player controls a classic Disney villain with their own unique deck, board, and win condition. Maleficent, Ursula, Jafar, and others all play completely differently, and players can use Fate cards to send heroes after their opponents' villains. A beautifully produced game that rewards knowing both your villain and your opponents.",
    viticulture: "Viticulture is a worker-placement game set in rustic Tuscany where players manage their own wineries. Plant vines, harvest grapes, age wine in your cellar, and fill wine orders to earn victory points. A Grande Worker lets you take spots already occupied, adding tension to the placement puzzle. Viticulture's accessible rules and charming theme make it one of the most beloved gateway-weight worker-placement games.",
    wanderingTowers: "Wandering Towers is a fast, whimsical game in which wizards race to reach the top of Desolate Tower first. Players draw and play cards to move their wizard or move the towers themselves — with shorter towers hiding inside taller ones. The constantly shifting tower formation creates delightful chaos and surprising reversals. A light, accessible game that plays quickly.",
    warChest: "War Chest is an area-control game that uses custom poker chips to represent units on the battlefield. Players draft unit coins from a bag and spend them to command units, recruit new troops, or control territory. Each unit type has a unique ability, and the drafting adds a push-your-luck element. Simple, elegant, and beautifully tactile.",
    warOfWhispers: "War of Whispers is a strategic area-control game in which players are secret agents of empires — but they don't control those empires directly. Instead, players secretly bet on which empires will dominate the world, then use their agents to influence the empires' decisions and manipulate the conflict to favor their bets. A devious game of hidden loyalty and indirect control.",
    wastelandExpress: "Wasteland Express Delivery Service is a post-apocalyptic pick-up-and-deliver game in which players drive armored trucks through a wasteland to complete delivery contracts, raid enemy camps, and upgrade their vehicles. The chaotic nature of the wasteland means the most efficient route isn't always the safest. A thematic and entertaining entry in the delivery game genre.",
    waterfallPark: "Waterfall Park is a tile-laying game in which players compete to build the most spectacular waterfall park. Place tiles to create winding waterfall paths, earn bonuses for long cascades, and score points based on the size and beauty of your completed park. A relaxing, family-friendly puzzle game with attractive components.",
    watergate: "Watergate is a tense two-player game based on the political scandal that brought down President Nixon. One player is the Nixon Administration, trying to protect key operatives; the other is the Washington Post, trying to gather enough evidence to force Nixon's resignation. A brilliant card-driven game of asymmetric information and political maneuvering.",
    wavelength: "Wavelength is a social guessing game in which a clue-giver must give a one-word clue to help their team guess where on a spectrum a hidden target lies. Spectrums like Hot vs. Cold or Legal vs. Illegal stretch between two extremes, and the clue must push the team toward the exact target position. A brilliant game of perspective and communication.",
    weDidntPlaytestThisAtAll: "We Didn't Playtest This at All is a deliberately chaotic card game in which the goal is simply to not lose — usually by not dying. Cards have absurd game-changing effects that can instantly win or lose the game, and strategy is largely irrelevant. Best played as a fast, hilarious filler between more serious games.",
    welcomeToYourPerfectHome: "Welcome To... is a flip-and-write game in which players are 1950s suburban architects designing their perfect neighborhood. Three cards are flipped each round and players choose one number-action combination to write on their personal sheet. Fill in house numbers, build pools, plant parks, and complete objectives to score the most points. A relaxing, nearly-simultaneous puzzle for any group size.",
    werewords: "Werewords is a social deduction word game in which players try to guess a secret word using yes-or-no questions. One player is the Mayor who knows the word; another is a Werewolf trying to secretly prevent the word from being guessed. If the village guesses the word, they can still lose if they can't identify the Werewolf. Blends word-guessing with social deduction for a fast, exciting experience.",
    wingspan: "Wingspan is an engine-building game in which players are bird enthusiasts attracting birds to their wildlife preserves. Each bird played extends a chain of actions in one of three habitats — forest, grassland, or wetland — and birds' special powers create increasingly powerful combos. With over 170 unique bird cards featuring real species and gorgeous artwork, Wingspan is a modern masterpiece.",
    wingspanAsia: "Wingspan Asia is both a standalone game and an expansion for Wingspan featuring birds of the Asian continent. As a standalone it supports up to 5 players or a new 2-player duet mode. As an expansion it adds new birds, a new habitat tray, and the exciting Flock mode for teams of 2. A worthy addition to the flock with the same beautiful design philosophy as the original.",
    witsAndWagers: "Wits and Wagers is a trivia game that doesn't require you to know the answers. Each round, players write down their best guess to a numerical question, then all guesses are laid out in order. Players bet on which guess they think is closest to the correct answer. The combination of trivia and betting means anyone can win regardless of knowledge.",
    worldsFair1893: "World's Fair 1893 is a set-collection and area-influence game set at the famous Chicago World's Fair. Players send supporters to attractions across the fairgrounds, collecting exhibit cards and gaining influence in five areas of the fair. At the end of each of three rounds, the player with the most influence in each area earns admission tickets. An elegant and thematic game of careful positioning.",
    xia: "Xia: Legends of a Drift System is a sandbox space adventure game in which players explore a modular hex-based galaxy, trading goods, completing missions, and battling each other across the stars. Each player commands a unique ship that can be upgraded and outfitted for any playstyle. With emergent storytelling, variable setup, and total freedom of action, Xia delivers an epic space opera experience.",
    yetiInMySpaghetti: "Yeti in My Spaghetti is a kids' dexterity game in which players carefully remove spaghetti noodles from a bowl while keeping the Yeti from falling in. Each player takes turns pulling a noodle from the pile; whoever causes the Yeti to fall loses. A simple, tactile, and charming game for young players.",
    zombieDice: "Zombie Dice is a quick push-your-luck dice game in which players are zombies trying to eat as many brains as possible. On your turn, randomly draw three dice and roll them to collect brains, shotgun blasts, or runners. Push your luck by rolling again, but three blasts and you lose all brains collected this turn. First to 13 wins.",

}

